All 120 tests pass. In isolated headless Chrome, local input overhead falls from 1.94 to 0.39 ms median. Paired Area 23 recorded-frame planning falls from 24.08 to 18.07 ms median (including navigation), with the same number of buffered forecasts. Both versions clear 12/12 simplified dasher courses at 660 speed and 135 ms configured delay; current has 176 versus 186 action changes and 45 versus 57 reversals. Total simulated clear time is 51.87 versus 52.30 seconds. See the newest `docs/recent-deaths.md` section and `artifacts/input-efficiency-review.json`, `input-batch-review.json`, and `profile-input-efficiency-cata23.json` for scope and evidence. These checks do not establish a live Cata clear or eliminate server/network jitter.

The preceding Area 23 death (`death-1790038871206.json`, revision `72dff445d360`) showed continued focused up-right movement 168 ms after an up-left request, despite a 125 ms delay estimate; the dasher prediction was accurate. Native submission/acknowledgement was not recorded then, so late delivery versus a missed intermediate turn could not be distinguished. Do not describe this input mismatch as fully solved. Restart the user's CLI to load this revision; do not attach to or interrupt their live browser for validation. Preserve the pre-Wacky profile, rescue behavior, unrelated local edits and ignored recordings.

