## Earlier update: pre-Wacky rollback

This update supersedes the implementation, validation and MM priorities below. The user requested a rollback because Wacky and subsequent enemy support degraded OOH/Catastrophic Core performance. The live observer/planner now use the earlier enemy handling, with existing timed routing, homing/dasher forecasts, browser attach and input fixes retained. Wacky learning, broad uncertainty regions, Switch activation, Sizing/Turning, Slippery, Pumpkin and teleport-specific forecasts have been removed. The CLI prints `Controller profile: pre-Wacky enemy handling` and records `controllerProfile: "pre-wacky"`.

The full newer implementation is preserved in local branch `backup/enemy-support-20260921` at commit `2b45647`; that branch has not been pushed by this task. The earliest Git commit already contained Wacky support, so this is a reconstructed source rollback using an older saved snapshot plus the earlier timed-routing changes, not an exact historical Git checkout. See `docs/pre-wacky-rollback.md` for provenance and validation. The active suite contains 97 checks; the removed model tests remain in the backup commit. Do not re-enable the MM expansion automatically. The rest of this handoff is historical context.

Validated rollback revision: `7bc9234b634f`. All 97 active tests and six generated courses passed; six short paired OOH 10/Catastrophic Core 35 replay windows survived. The on-time replay medians fell from 11.75 to 8.67 ms (OOH) and 20.06 to 15.66 ms (Cata) with identical simulated path outcomes. Offline Chrome P/Escape/observation checks passed. Fresh live runs remain unverified. Rollback edits are local working-tree changes at the end of this task and must be transferred/committed separately from the earlier handoff commit.

## Start here

The user wants to repeatedly run Monumental Migration (MM), analyze each death, fix its underlying cause, add a meaningful regression where the evidence permits, and retry. Preserve fast forward progress: excessive retreating, Shift use and unnecessary turns have also been recurring complaints. Successful short replays are evidence for a particular encounter, not proof of a full clear or elimination of every failure mode.

The latest request was to prepare this handoff before switching machines. Work on the run-and-review loop was interrupted at the investigation stage. **No automatic MM restart, death-watching daemon, or unattended AI analysis was implemented.** The existing controller records deaths; analysis and fixes currently require an active assistant session.

