## Reference documents and source refresh

- `README.md`: run options, input behavior and architecture.
- `docs/enemy-types.md`: generated full enemy/projectile directory.
- `docs/enemy-catalog.md`: implemented behavior and limits.
- `docs/enemy-simulations.md`: suite scope and how to extend it.
- `docs/monumental-migration.md`: video timestamps, MM families and priorities.
- `docs/recent-deaths.md`: detailed historical diagnoses and validation evidence.

Catalog source: https://evades.io/index.e75284cc.js

Rebuild the same catalog from the copied source:

```sh
python3 scripts/build-enemy-catalog.py \
  --source artifacts/public-client-index.e75284cc.js \
  --url https://evades.io/index.e75284cc.js
```

Running `python3 scripts/build-enemy-catalog.py` without a local source fetches the currently published client. It parses data literals without executing the client. Review ID/schema changes before using a refreshed catalog with existing code.

Video inspection used temporary `uv` environments for yt-dlp, Pillow and PyObjC Vision, plus ffmpeg. These are not runtime dependencies. The saved frames/index are sufficient to resume the reference review; no need to repeat the download or OCR.
